    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2EwgfBq4oNgk7vQeDSgUsdE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: touches `sp-org-babel` (doc and module) and three doc mentions.\n- Merge in any order; no PR depends on it and it depends on none.\n\n## What and why\n\n- `M-x check-tangle` did not exist; #534 mentioned it, but only `tools/check-tangle.sh` did.\n- New `sp-check-tangle` in `sp-org-babel` (next to `sp-tangle-changed`), with `check-tangle` as an alias.\n  - Runs `tools/check-tangle.sh` from `user-emacs-directory` with `compilation-start`, so Emacs stays usable.\n  - Output goes to `*sp-check-tangle*`; the echo area says `passed` or `FAILED`.\n  - `g` in the buffer re-runs it.\n  - `user-error` if the script is missing or not executable.\n  - `sp-check-tangle-script` holds the script path.\n- Docs (bullets): new section in `docs/tangles/text/sp-org-babel.org`, plus mentions in `docs/tangling-instructions.org`, `README.org` and `docs/architecture/stable-and-sandbox-emacs.org`.\n- Reminder: the script leaves the tangled files in the working tree; `git diff` shows the drift, `git checkout -- libraries` undoes it.\n\n## What was and was not run\n\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: loaded the module, ran `sp-check-tangle`; with an uncommitted edit it ended `exited abnormally` and printed `FAILED`.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh` on the committed branch: `All tangled modules match their docs.`\n- Not run: interactive Emacs, the Stow-symlinked `~/.config/emacs-modular` (the script needs `user-emacs-directory` to be inside the git checkout).\n\n## Manual testing checklist\n\n- [ ] Reload `sp-org-babel` (or restart Emacs).\n- [ ] `M-x check-tangle` on a clean checkout: `*sp-check-tangle*` opens, ends `finished`, echo area says `passed`.\n- [ ] Edit a module `.el` by hand, run it again: `exited abnormally`, echo area says `FAILED`, the buffer lists the module.\n- [ ] `git checkout -- libraries` afterwards restores the files.\n- [ ] `g` in `*sp-check-tangle*` re-runs the check.\n- [ ] Emacs stays usable while it runs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBHDxLWJbbDGCDRzAp)_",
